==========================================================================
(3) HARD CORE map: fraction of primitive sets where E2 >= main (bound fails)
==========================================================================
  n=5: E2>=main (bound fails) for 0/150 primitive sets; those have SMALL minimal resonance, e.g. []
  n=6: E2>=main (bound fails) for 0/150 primitive sets; those have SMALL minimal resonance, e.g. []

  => the rigorous bound E(v)<main PROVES LRC for the decorrelated majority (large
     minimal resonance); the hard core (E>=main) is the small-minimal-resonance
     sets, led by the AP/regular polygon. Progress = LRC reduced to bounding the
     resonance energy of the small-minimal-resonance core (the returns, S545).
